## IAM Instance Profile

1. What is an IAM Instance Profile?

An IAM Instance Profile is a container that allows an EC2 instance to use an IAM Role.

I know you guyzz are thinking that Why IAM Instance profile allow Ec2 to use An IAM role. Because Ec2 Instance Can not use Iam role directly. The instance 
profile is the connector that allows the role to be attached to the instance. 

EC2
|
Instance Profile
|
IAM Role
|
Permissions

## Why do we need it?
 Suppose an Ec2 instance needs to access an s3 bucket.

 Instead of storing Aws keys inside ec2. 
  like-> ec2 -> access keys -> s3 bucket.
I use Instance profile, because it attached IAM role with Ec2
  like-> ec2 -> instance profile -> IAM role -> s3 bucket

Actually this allow ec2 store temporary credential and avoid storing aws crendentials  long term on server.

## Instance Profile vs IAM Role 
  IAM ROle 
    Defines: 
      1. Trust policy -> Who can asssume role?
      2. Permissions -> What role can do?
  
  Instance Profile
  Allows:
    Ec2 to use that IAM Role. 
 
 